From 13773dc1453aa5756d59e1442af9cf93cfa11828 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: George Watson <george@hellas.ai>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 12:50:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] usb: dwc2: cv1800: let DT drive g_dma/host_dma
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream dwc2's CV1800 match callback hard-codes DMA off, which forces
slave/PIO mode and the gadget TX path wedges after a handful of packets.
The vendor 5.10 kernel enables DMA (via g-use-dma DT prop + g_dma = 1 in
its own cv182x callback).

Drop the two '= false' assignments so the DT's g-use-dma property drives
g_dma/host_dma — this matches how other dwc2 platforms (rockchip, etc.)
operate, and lets per-board DT decide whether DMA is usable.

Signed-off-by: George Watson <george@hellas.ai>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
index 091bfcfef..94ce6f738 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
@@ -224,8 +224,6 @@ static void dwc2_set_cv1800_params(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 
 	p->otg_caps.hnp_support = false;
 	p->otg_caps.srp_support = false;
-	p->host_dma = false;
-	p->g_dma = false;
 	p->speed = DWC2_SPEED_PARAM_HIGH;
 	p->phy_type = DWC2_PHY_TYPE_PARAM_UTMI;
 	p->phy_utmi_width = 16;
-- 
